    "answer": {
      "short": "$6343$.\n\nThe digit sum is $16$, the first two digits give $63$, the first and third give $64=8^2$, and the second and fourth give $33$.",
      "worked": "Write the digits as $a,b,c,d$. The two-digit multiples of $11$ have equal digits, so $b=d$. The possible two-digit squares $ac$ are $16,25,36,49,64,81$. Requiring $ab$ to be divisible by $9$ gives the corresponding candidates $1868,2757,3666,4595,6343,8111$. Their digit sums are respectively $23,21,21,23,16,11$. Only $6343$ has an even digit sum. Its other conditions are satisfied because $63=9\\times7$, $64=8^2$ and $33=11\\times3$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
